  "id": "invariant-sequence",
  "term": "invariant sequence",
  "definition": "In this context, an invariant sequence means a fixed or consistent order in which functions recover, regardless of the individual. Here it refers to whether cognitive and neurobehavioral abilities return in the same pattern across different people after general anesthesia.",
